values ('c8d9e0f1-2a3b-4d98-9e78-9f0a1b2c3d88', 'social-psychology-sociological', 'Social Psychology (Sociological)', 'Social Psychology (Sociological) examines how selves, identities, emotions, attitudes, roles, groups, power, inequality, and collective action are produced through social interaction. Unlike a primarily individual-cognitive version of social psychology, this course emphasizes symbolic interaction, identity theory, dramaturgy, status processes, socialization, culture, networks, organizations, and institutions. Students learn to connect micro-level interaction with macro-level social structure.');

